From 4ab126aa8256a6ff40e634aebf918ba7262b3d4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:12:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 60 fps step 1: map camera, map sprites, mist, snow and
 Ninjamon in the late tick

renderMap scrolled the camera (tickCameraFollowPlayer, with its VRAM tile
uploads and DrawSync), checked the daytime transition, animated the map
sprites, mist and snow (snow drew from the gameplay rand()) and stored
CAMERA_*_PREVIOUS. All of that is now lateTickMap, the late tick of the map
object 0xFA0, in the same order; renderMap only builds the tile and sprite
prims.

The map sprites were advanced after each one's prim was built, so the late
tick (tickMapOverlays) first records what the render has to draw this tick
(frame, position, layer, kind) and then advances: renderMapOverlays draws
exactly what the original drew. Snowflakes move x before drawing and y after,
plus a per-tick jitter, also recorded. The Ninjamon effect (object 0xFBA,
render only, moved the sprites with randomLimit) becomes a late tick.

rand() is consumed once per tick by the snow, as with one render per tick.

